WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.002 size:81% position:41%
-Our next guests are
Emmy-nominated writers

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:04.137 size:88% position:44%
whose work you know from
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:05.071 line:92%
Their new show, "The Other Two,"

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
premieres Thursday night
on Comedy Central.

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:08.308 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:12.412
-Hey, guys, it's your captains
speaking -- Tiff and Amanda.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.513 line:92%
Sorry about the turbulence,

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:17.083
but from now on we're expecting
such a smooth ride.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.219 line:92%
So relax and enjoy the flight.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.687 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Bye!

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.921 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, no.

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:25.158 line:92%
Our pilot's name is Tiff?

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, what, a woman
can't be a pilot?

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-Wow, gay misogyny is real.

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, a woman can be my pilot,
all right?

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:35.668
Meryl Streep can be my pilot.
Viola Davis can be my pilot.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.505
-You'd rather have Viola Davis,
the actress,

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:40.707 size:84% position:42% line:92%
than two actual pilots?

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.342 line:92%
-Hey, guys, sorry to bug,

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:45.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we have now reached
cruising altitude.

00:00:45.245 --> 00:00:49.082
-So, feel free to unbuckle
and move about the cabin.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:49.616 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Bye!

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:52.685
-I know you know what I mean.
-No. No, I don't. I don't.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.788 line:92%
-They said bye at the same time.

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:56.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome to the show
my friends

00:00:56.589 --> 00:00:58.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
Chris Kelly and
Sarah Schneider, everyone!

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.794 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:15.542 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:16.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
Welcome, you two!
-Wow!

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:19.679
-Oh, my God!
-I'm so happy to have you here.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have been friends
for a long time,

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:24.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we all wrote together
at "Saturday Night Live."

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:25.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-We did.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you were head writers
together

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
during the election year
of 2016.

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.123 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-We absolutely were.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:32.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, I was a head writer
during 2008,

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:35.195
which was similar in that
it was a bit of a circus.

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:38.798
The difference was, on election
night, the circus ended.

00:01:38.798 --> 00:01:41.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-In 2008.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
But not for you guys.
-No.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:45.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You had to keep writing
all those sketches.

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:47.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know. We would keep trying
to write, like --

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:50.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
we love writing nostalgic
sketches about, like,

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:52.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
going home
and high school theater.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:54.447 size:88% position:44%
And we would keep trying
to write those sketches.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:58.184
And every single week, we would
be on the set loving it,

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:00.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like, our phones
would buzz.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:02.489 line:92%
-We'd be like, "It's him again."

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:03.022 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:05.625
"He has ruined our week for us."
-The fun is over.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, so, you did a sketch
that I love

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
called "Crucible Cast Party."
-Yeah.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:12.799 size:88% position:44%
-This might actually be
you checking your phone.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:13.466 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-This is mid-moment.

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.802
-Okay. So, what were you seeing
on your phone?

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:19.038
-So, we were making
a fun musical with all the girls

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.474 line:92%
about a high school party.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.209 line:92%
And then we got the alert --

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:26.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
the "Access Hollywood" tape
had come out.

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:26.980 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:29.849
-And so, we were both just like,
"Oh, God damn it!"

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:31.551 line:92%
So, that's a photo of one woman

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
having a blast
making a music video.

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.289 size:84% position:42%
And then another man
in the deepest of hells

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:39.959
trying to write a cold open
in 45 minutes on Friday night

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.995
at 3:00 in the morning.
-Yes, because things were

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:45.031
happening that you had to throw
away what you had for Saturday

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:48.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
on Friday, which rarely
happened in my time there.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:48.668 size:75% position:38% line:92%
This was also great.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys wrote
the Bernie Sanders sketches

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:54.741
where Larry David played Bernie
Sanders, which is fantastic.

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:55.275 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:59.846 size:88% position:44%
Such a wonderful person,
but before you meet him,

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
you think he might be, like,
really irascible

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.650 line:92%
and maybe not fun to work with.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he was great, right?
-He was lovely.

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
We did this
"Bern your enthusiasm" parody,

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:10.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
and on Saturday night,
right before dress, we heard,

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:13.059 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, Larry wants to come up
and watch a cut of the video."

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:16.429
And we were like, "Oh, no,
I don't want that to happen.

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.197 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I don't want to watch us

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:19.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
do a parody of his own show
next to him."

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:20.600 line:92%
It was very nerve-racking,

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he laughed
through the whole thing

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:23.736 line:92%
and was so positive and nice.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.906
And I was like, "This isn't how
you're supposed to be.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:27.740 line:92%
You're supposed to hate this."

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.743
-Well, he did send us an e-mail
afterwards that was titled,

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Thanks," and basically
the gist of it was,

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:35.582
"I had a great time except for
all of the packing and flying.

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:38.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I like you guys
but I don't really want to see

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:39.319 size:78% position:39% line:92%
you guys again soon."

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:40.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And we were like,
"There he is."

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:43.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's what we signed up for.
-That's what we wanted.

